{"ts":"2026-07-25T12:10:49.472Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-wdrkfr"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-708: make retained delete tombstones discoverable and policy-controlled"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Expose history streams retained after pm delete as intentional tombstones through supported health/list output, explain retention in delete results/help, and define explicit opt-in retention or garbage-collection policy without weakening append-only audit defaults."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:history","area:storage","delete","gc","gh-issue","multi-agent","observability"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:10:49.472Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:10:49.472Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm health or an equivalent supported command reports a bounded count/list of history streams without live item files and distinguishes valid delete tombstones from corruption; pm delete output and help explicitly state that the history stream is retained; an opt-in tombstone retention or gc policy is documented and cannot silently remove append-only proof; SDK/CLI contracts expose the same structured tombstone state; sandboxed delete, health, history, gc, and merge regression tests preserve 100% coverage"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Deleted-item audit streams are visible, explainable, and bounded by an explicit retention policy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Agents can distinguish intentional audit proof from orphaned residue and can manage long-lived multi-agent workspace growth without raw filesystem inspection"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-o2kc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-25T12:10:49.472Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate-check evidence: all-status search and full metadata review covered closed delete implementation pm-4yl0,closed storage observability plan pm-l709,open history namespace work pm-tqel,open mutation-completeness gate pm-9yfo,parent epic pm-o2kc,and closed delete/modify merge fix pm-wwfd. Those items own delete execution,generic storage stats,command naming,append completeness,durability,and resurrection detection respectively; none owns enumeration/explanation/retention policy for legitimate history-only tombstones. GH-708 is the canonical new owner."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"95eb8bcaeb566e9db52c57ba56a7eb50b5efa628176f8f46e470191873ca2ba7","message":""}
